        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: مصدوم",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مصدوم (masdum) — \"injured; an injured person\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مصدوم (masdum) را با آمبولانس به بیمارستان بردند. Masdum râ bâ âmbulâns be bimârestân bordand. They took the injured man to hospital by ambulance."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In news reports; plural masdumân or masdumin."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "masdum is usually traced to Arabic maṣdūm, \"struck\", a participle of the same root as ṣadma \"a blow\"; EtymDB lists no entry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
